# Letin Severine (bouyonmusique.com, wave 11 parity, 2026-10-20)
# THIN DOSSIER: after full research, Letin Severine has no verified biography, no solo release and no performer credit anywhere consulted. Her entire verified public record is a songwriting and composition credit, always alongside Letin Sylia, on four Yellow Gaza / Yellow Gaza Girls tracks between 2013 and 2025. This profile publishes exactly that record, track by track, and invents nothing.
# Sources used:
# - Shazam, Yellow Gaza "Vole Nonm a Moun" (opened 2026-10-20): single released March 5, 2013, label Yellow Gaza, language French, BPM 157; credits list Yellow Gaza as performer and songwriter, Letin Sylia as composer and Letin Severine as composer. Deezer "Bouyon bass" playlist (opened 2026-10-20) gives the same track at 03:40 with composers Letin Sylia and Letin Severine.
# - Shazam, Yellow Gaza "Sa ki bon (Bouyon King)" (opened 2026-10-20): single released December 14, 2021, label Vadore Concept, BPM 157; credits list VADORE CONCEPT GROUPE as composer, Letin Sylia as songwriter and Letin Severine as songwriter. Deezer gives duration 02:42 and writers Letin Sylia and Letin Severine.
# - Shazam, Yellow Gaza and Yumei "PLAN A 3 (feat. Yu Mei) [Femmes Fatales Edition Bouyon]" (opened 2026-10-20): single released September 7, 2024, label Vadore Concept Groupe, language French, BPM 157; credits list MEYAPIN BORDIN ALLAN as composer, LETIN SYLVIA as songwriter, Letin Severine as songwriter and TITINE EMMANUELLE as songwriter.
# - Shazam, Yellow Gaza Girls "LEVRETTE" (opened 2026-10-20): single released October 16, 2025, label Vadore Concept Groupe, BPM 160; credits list Christophe Democrite as composer, Letin Severine as songwriter, LETIN SYLVIA as songwriter, and VADOR CONCEPT GROUP as producer.
# - Viberate, Yellow Gaza artist page (search result, 2026-10-20): presents Yellow Gaza as an artist from Guadeloupe and lists "Sa ki bon (Bouyon King)", "Vole Nonm A Moun" and "V.N.M II" among his known songs. Used only to place the performing act, never as biography of Letin Severine.
# - BBC 1Xtra listing for Seani B Top Selector Mix by Klonde (search result, 2026-10-20): the mix, billed as bringing Bouyon (Dominica) and Dennery Segment vibes, includes Yellow Gaza "Vole Nonm a Moun" in its music played list. Used only as a broadcast trace of that one track.
# - Disambiguation: the famous singer Severine, winner of Eurovision 1971 for Monaco, is a different published artist (Josiane Grizeau, born in Paris in 1948, per her Shazam artist page consulted 2026-10-20). No source consulted links her to Letin Severine, and no fact from her biography is used here.
# - Relationship note: no source consulted states any family link, duo status or shared biography between Letin Severine and Letin Sylia. They are documented only as recurring co-credits. No origin town, no date of birth and no official account were verified for Letin Severine, so sameAs stays empty.

